        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 1:24PM PDT by NWS Spokane WA</headline>
        <description>At 124 PM PDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 24
miles west of Omak, moving northeast at 10 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

This storm will remain over mainly rural areas of central Okanogan
County.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
